{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792170963,"nonce":"xedShNda2J70yfU6m2rRsp9XCQA=","message":"Checked every text-measurement cache in the chain, ruling out a simple cache-key collision:\n- ashui's own GlyphOutlines.hx kept Map: keyed by family|generic|weight|italic|size|letterSpacing|lineHeight|text. size is in the key.\n- blinc_text's LayoutCacheKey (crates/blinc_text/src/renderer.rs), both construction sites (prepare_text_internal and prepare_styled_text): both include font_size_bits (f32::to_bits, byte-exact) in the key, separate from font_id.\n- blinc_layout's text.rs stores measured_width per node (self.measured_width), not in a cross-node map.\n\nSo whatever is happening is not \"two different sizes hash to the same cache slot\" in any of these three places. Remaining hypotheses, not yet checked: something stateful in fallback face resolution (FallbackFaces::resolve / the fallbacks: u8 signature field — loads lazily, order/state-dependent); a shared mutable scratch buffer somewhere in the shaping path that isn't part of a cache key at all; or something in Taffy's own measure-function caching on the blinc_layout side I haven't located yet. Next step should be an isolated repro (a Rust unit test in blinc_text or blinc_layout with two TextElements, same content, different font_size, asserting both measured_width values independently) rather than more static reading — I don't have strong enough evidence past this point to keep guessing.","files":null}]}